.IX Title "SURFRAW-UPDATE-PATH 1"
.TH SURFRAW-UPDATE-PATH 1 2024-09-09 "perl v5.40.0" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "نام (NAME)"
surfraw\-update\-path \- updates PATH in shell config files
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
surfraw-update-path [\fB\-add\fR] [\fB\-remove\fR] [\fB\-check\fR] [\fB\-sys\fR] [\fB\-all\fR] [\fB\-help\fR] [\fB\-shell\fR=\fISHELL\fR]
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
surfraw-update-path adds the surfraw elvi directory (/usr/lib/surfraw) to
your PATH in your shell's config file.
.PP
Currently it supports \fBbash\fR, \fBsh\fR, \fBcsh\fR, \fBtcsh\fR, \fBash\fR,
\&\fBdash\fR, \fBksh\fR, \fBpdksh\fR, \fBzsh\fR, \fBrc\fR, and \fBes\fR
.PP
Don't forget to login again or source your login files for it to take
effect.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.IX Header "OPTIONS"
.IP \fB\-check\fR 4
.IX Item "-check"
Checks to see if the surfraw config code is present.
This is the default.
.IP \fB\-add\fR 4
.IX Item "-add"
Adds the surfraw config code.
.IP \fB\-remove\fR 4
.IX Item "-remove"
Removes the surfraw config code
.IP \fB\-sys\fR 4
.IX Item "-sys"
Updates the system-wide shell config instead of the user.
Must be done as root.
.IP \fB\-shell\fR=\fISHELL\fR 4
.IX Item "-shell=SHELL"
Selects the shell to configure. Defaults to the value of the \f(CW$SHELL\fR
environment variable.
.Sp
Currently supported shells are:
.Sp
\&\fBsh\fR, \fBash\fR, \fBbash\fR, \fBdash\fR, \fBcsh\fR, \fBtcsh\fR, \fBksh\fR, \fBpdksh\fR,
\&\fBzsh\fR, \fBrc\fR, and \fBes\fR.
.IP \fB\-all\fR 4
.IX Item "-all"
Attempts to configure the startup files for all known shells
.IP \fB\-help\fR 4
.IX Item "-help"
Gives a usage message
.SH "RETURN VALUE"
.IX Header "RETURN VALUE"
\&\-check returns 0 if the surfraw code is present in the file, 1 if it
is not found, or 2 on error.
.PP
All other options return 0 on success, or 2 on error.
.SH "محیط (ENVIRONMENT)"
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
.IP SHELL 4
.IX Item "SHELL"
Used to determine which shell to configure, if \fB\-shell\fR is not given.
.IP HOME 4
.IX Item "HOME"
Used to find users config files.
.IP ENV 4
.IX Item "ENV"
Used by posix-compliant shells to specify a startup rc file.
.IP ZDOTDIR 4
.IX Item "ZDOTDIR"
Used to find user config files for zsh. If not set, defaults to HOME.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\fBsurfraw\fR\|(1), \fBsh\fR\|(1), \fBash\fR\|(1), \fBbash\fR\|(1), \fBdash\fR\|(1), \fBcsh\fR\|(1), \fBtcsh\fR\|(1), \fBksh\fR\|(1),
\&\fBpdksh\fR\|(1), \fBzsh\fR\|(1), \fBrc\fR\|(1), \fBes\fR\|(1)
.SH "نویسنده (AUTHOR)"
.IX Header "AUTHOR"
Ian Beckwith <ianb@erislabs.net>
